{"id":29031,"slug":"-round-midnight","title":"’Round Midnight","year":1986,"country":"United States, France","duration":131,"spine":1122,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29031--round-midnight","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/f0d131afa79169e59ab41e5c64b0070b/Bu1NdqFyV6gvXhif42Ey2qkSVzbyAu_large.jpg","description":"’Round Midnight is a love letter from director Bertrand Tavernier to the heyday of bebop and the Black American musicians who found refuge in the smoky underground jazz clubs of 1950s Paris. In a sui generis, Oscar-nominated fusion of performer and character, legendary saxophonist Dexter Gordon plays Dale Turner, a brilliant New York jazz veteran whose music aches with beauty but whose personal life is ravaged by addiction. Searching for a fresh start in Paris, Turner strikes up an unlikely friendship with a struggling single father and ardent jazz fan (François Cluzet) who finds his life transformed as he attempts to help the self-destructive musician. Herbie Hancock’s evocative, Oscar-winning score sets the mood for this definitive jazz film, a bittersweet opus that glows with lived-in, soulful authenticity.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Bertrand Tavernier","slug":"bertrand-tavernier"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Dexter Gordon","role":"Dale Turner","slug":"dexter-gordon"},{"actor":"François Cluzet","role":"Francis Borier","slug":"francois-cluzet"},{"actor":"Gabrielle Haker","role":"Berangere","slug":"gabrielle-haker"},{"actor":"Sandra Reaves-Phiillips","role":"Buttercup","slug":"sandra-reaves-phiillips"},{"actor":"Lonette McKee","role":"Darcey Leigh","slug":"lonette-mckee"},{"actor":"Christine Pascal","role":"Sylvie","slug":"christine-pascal"},{"actor":"Herbie Hancock","role":"Eddie Wayne","slug":"herbie-hancock"},{"actor":"Bobbie Hutcherson","role":"Ace","slug":"bobbie-hutcherson"},{"actor":"Martin Scorsese","role":"Goodley","slug":"martin-scorsese"},{"actor":"John Berry","role":"Ben","slug":"john-berry"}],"credi